# @repo/{{ name }}

Internal workspace package at `{{ pathPrefix }}/{{ name }}`.

Consumed as TypeScript source through its `exports` map — there is no build step.
Import it as `@repo/{{ name }}` after adding `"@repo/{{ name }}": "workspace:*"` to
the consuming workspace's dependencies.

## Commands

| Command | What it does |
|---|---|
| `bun run lint` | Biome check for this package (no ESLint, no Prettier) |
| `bun run typecheck` | `tsc --noEmit` |
| `bun run test` | Unit tests in `src/**/__tests__/*.test.ts` |

Run `bun run format` from the repo root to apply fixes across the monorepo.

## Conventions

- Unit tests live beside the code in `src/**/__tests__/*.test.ts`.
- Integration tests (anything touching Postgres, Redis, or the bucket) go in
  `tests/integration/*.test.ts` and run via a separate `test:integration` script.
  The two directories must stay disjoint — `bun test <path>` filters by substring.
{{#if needsEnv}}- This package owns its environment variables in `src/env.ts` and exposes them
  via the `./env` subpath. Apps compose them with `extends: [...]` in their own
  `env.ts`. Add any new variable to `src/env.ts` **and** every consuming app's
  `.env.example` in the same commit.
{{/if}}
See [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) for the full set of repo conventions.
